  "final_message": "I added `amountCents` and `createdAt` to `OrderPlaced`, but I didn't remove `totalCents` and `placedAt`. A straight rename would break billing-service and analytics-ingest, which read those fields today, and ARCH-4 says renames must go through deprecation. All 39 tests pass and the architecture check finds no new violations; it still reports the one known violation it already ignored.\n\n**What changed**\n- **`src/core/events.ts`:** `OrderPlaced` now has `amountCents` and `createdAt`, set to the same values as `totalCents` and `placedAt`. The two old fields are marked `@deprecated` with a note pointing to their replacements.\n- **`schemaVersion` stays at 3.** Adding fields doesn't break consumers, and changing the version could break any consumer that checks for exactly 3.\n- **Tests** in `test/app.test.ts` and `test/adapters.test.ts` now check both the old and new fields, including in the serialized Kafka payload.\n\n**What I left alone**\n- **The `GET /orders/{id}` and `POST /orders` responses** still return `totalCents` and `placedAt`. You asked about the event, and web-storefront depends on the API response staying backward compatible (ARCH-8).\n- **The internal `Order` model, cursors, and the payments request** are unchanged. The payments request already uses `amountMinor`.\n\n**To finish the rename**\n1. Ask the billing-service and analytics-ingest owners to switch to `amountCents` and `createdAt`.\n2. Once both have deployed the switch, remove `totalCents` and `placedAt` from the event. That removal is a breaking change, so it should probably also move `schemaVersion` to 4.\n\nIf your team has a formal deprecation process, such as a changelog entry, a notice in the event catalog, or a removal date, that should be done too. I haven't done it because none of it is in this repo.",
